# Conditional proof (CP) and indirect proof (IP), which the 2018 engine did
# not have. ACP and AIP open a subproof with an assumption; CP and IP close
# the innermost open one on the next line, citing it as a range. The lines of
# a subproof are indented here only to make them easier to read.
# The format is described in ../README.md.

# --- Conditional proof: assumption p, ..., q ∴ p → q ---

case: cp-absorption
source: CP added in 2026
problem: {P → Q=>P → (P & Q)}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q ; 1,2 MP
4.   P & Q ; 2,3 CONJ
5. P → (P & Q) ; 2-4 CP
expect: valid

case: cp-irrelevant-antecedent
source: CP added in 2026
problem: {Q=>P → Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q & P ; 1,2 CONJ
4.   Q ; 3 SIMP
5. P → Q ; 2-4 CP
expect: valid

case: cp-nested
source: CP added in 2026, proving exportation
problem: {(P & Q) → R=>P → (Q → R)}
2.   P ; ACP
3.     Q ; ACP
4.     P & Q ; 2,3 CONJ
5.     R ; 1,4 MP
6.   Q → R ; 3-5 CP
7. P → (Q → R) ; 2-6 CP
expect: valid

case: cp-theorem-identity
source: CP added in 2026, a theorem with no premises
problem: {=>P → P}
1.   P ; ACP
2. P → P ; 1-1 CP
expect: valid

case: cp-theorem-hypothetical-syllogism
source: CP added in 2026, a theorem with no premises
problem: {=>(P → Q) → ((Q → R) → (P → R))}
1.   P → Q ; ACP
2.     Q → R ; ACP
3.     P → R ; 1,2 HS
4.   (Q → R) → (P → R) ; 2-3 CP
5. (P → Q) → ((Q → R) → (P → R)) ; 1-4 CP
expect: valid

case: cp-with-ug
source: CP added in 2026
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → Gx)=>(∀x)Fx → (∀x)Gx}
2.   (∀x)Fx ; ACP
3.   Fy ; 2 UI
4.   Fy → Gy ; 1 UI
5.   Gy ; 4,3 MP
6.   (∀x)Gx ; 5 UG
7. (∀x)Fx → (∀x)Gx ; 2-6 CP
expect: valid

case: cp-then-ug
source: CP added in 2026
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → Gx)//(∀x)(Gx → Hx)=>(∀x)(Fx → Hx)}
3.   Fy ; ACP
4.   Fy → Gy ; 1 UI
5.   Gy ; 4,3 MP
6.   Gy → Hy ; 2 UI
7.   Hy ; 6,5 MP
8. Fy → Hy ; 3-7 CP
9. (∀x)(Fx → Hx) ; 8 UG
expect: valid

# --- Indirect proof: assumption p, ..., q & ~q ∴ ~p (or q when p is ~q) ---

case: ip-basic
source: IP added in 2026
problem: {P → Q//P → ~Q=>~P}
3.   P ; AIP
4.   Q ; 1,3 MP
5.   ~Q ; 2,3 MP
6.   Q & ~Q ; 4,5 CONJ
7. ~P ; 3-6 IP
expect: valid

case: ip-negated-assumption
source: IP added in 2026
problem: {P | Q//~Q=>P}
3.   ~P ; AIP
4.   Q ; 1,3 DS
5.   Q & ~Q ; 4,2 CONJ
6. P ; 3-5 IP
expect: valid

case: ip-excluded-middle
source: IP added in 2026, a theorem with no premises
problem: {=>P | ~P}
1.   ~(P | ~P) ; AIP
2.   ~P & ~~P ; 1 DM
3. P | ~P ; 1-2 IP
expect: valid

case: ip-contradiction-reversed
source: IP added in 2026
problem: {P → Q//P → ~Q=>~P}
3.   P ; AIP
4.   Q ; 1,3 MP
5.   ~Q ; 2,3 MP
6.   ~Q & Q ; 5,4 CONJ
7. ~P ; 3-6 IP
strict: invalid at 7: IP needs the subproof to end in p & ~p, and ~Q & Q has the negation first
flexible: valid

case: ip-with-quantifiers
source: IP added in 2026
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → Gx)//(∃x)Fx=>(∃x)Gx}
3.   ~(∃x)Gx ; AIP
4.   (∀x)~Gx ; 3 QN
5.   Fa ; 2 EI
6.   Fa → Ga ; 1 UI
7.   Ga ; 6,5 MP
8.   ~Ga ; 4 UI
9.   Ga & ~Ga ; 7,8 CONJ
10. (∃x)Gx ; 3-9 IP
expect: valid

# --- Scope errors ---

case: cite-inside-closed-subproof
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {P → Q=>Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q ; 1,2 MP
4. P → Q ; 2-3 CP
5. Q ; 1,2 MP
expect: invalid at 5: line 2 is inside the subproof on lines 2-3, which is closed
argument: invalid

case: assumption-never-discharged
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {P → Q=>Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q ; 1,2 MP
expect: invalid at end: the assumption on line 2 is never discharged
argument: invalid

case: cp-from-a-line-that-is-not-an-assumption
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {Q=>P → Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q & P ; 1,2 CONJ
4.   Q ; 3 SIMP
5. P → Q ; 3-4 CP
expect: invalid at 5: line 3 is not an assumption, so no subproof starts there

case: cp-range-ends-early
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {Q=>P → Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q & P ; 1,2 CONJ
4.   Q ; 3 SIMP
5. P → (Q & P) ; 2-3 CP
expect: invalid at 5: CP closes the subproof right after its last line, so the range must end at line 4

case: cp-wrong-conditional
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {Q=>P → Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q & P ; 1,2 CONJ
4.   Q ; 3 SIMP
5. Q → P ; 2-4 CP
expect: invalid at 5: CP on lines 2-4 gives P → Q

case: cp-closes-the-outer-subproof-first
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {(P & Q) → R=>P → (Q → R)}
2.   P ; ACP
3.     Q ; ACP
4.     P & Q ; 2,3 CONJ
5.     R ; 1,4 MP
6. P → R ; 2-5 CP
expect: invalid at 6: the assumption on line 3 is still open; close its subproof first

case: cp-closes-a-subproof-twice
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {Q=>P → Q}
2.   P ; ACP
3.   Q & P ; 1,2 CONJ
4.   Q ; 3 SIMP
5. P → Q ; 2-4 CP
6. P → Q ; 2-5 CP
expect: invalid at 6: the subproof that starts on line 2 is already closed

case: cp-cites-a-line
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {=>P → P}
1.   P ; ACP
2. P → P ; 1 CP
expect: invalid at 2: CP cites the subproof it closes, as a range like 3-5

case: acp-with-a-citation
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {P=>P → P}
2.   P ; 1 ACP
3. P → P ; 2-2 CP
expect: invalid at 2: ACP cites no lines

case: range-for-another-rule
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 1-2 CONJ
expect: invalid at 3: only CP and IP cite a range of lines

case: ip-without-contradiction
source: soundness, IP added in 2026
problem: {P | Q=>P}
2.   ~P ; AIP
3.   Q ; 1,2 DS
4. P ; 2-3 IP
expect: invalid at 4: IP needs the subproof to end in a contradiction, p & ~p, and line 3 is not one
argument: invalid

case: ug-free-in-open-assumption
source: soundness, CP added in 2026
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → Gx)=>Fy → (∀x)Gx}
2.   Fy ; ACP
3.   Fy → Gy ; 1 UI
4.   Gy ; 3,2 MP
5.   (∀x)Gx ; 4 UG
6. Fy → (∀x)Gx ; 2-5 CP
expect: invalid at 5: UG cannot generalize y, which is free in the assumption on line 2
argument: invalid
